module: support-ticket

purpose:
  Let a small team move customer problems from first report to resolution without losing any.

rules:
  - A ticket is always in exactly one state: open, in-progress, waiting-on-customer, resolved or closed.
  - A ticket moves open to in-progress, in-progress to waiting-on-customer or resolved, waiting-on-customer back to in-progress, and resolved to closed.
  - A ticket cannot jump from open straight to resolved or closed.
  - A closed ticket cannot change state.

workflow: move-ticket
  input:
    ticket-title
  output:
    The ticket is in its new state, or the person is told that the move is not allowed.

example: start-work
  given:
    An open ticket.
  when:
    A team member starts work on it.
  then:
    The ticket is in-progress.

example: skip-ahead
  given:
    An open ticket.
  when:
    A team member marks it resolved.
  then:
    The system refuses and says the ticket must be in-progress first.

uncertainty: reopening
  blocking: yes
  question:
    Can a resolved or closed ticket be reopened if the customer writes back?
